  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ODA Technical Assistance Facility to build LMIC capacity and establish links with UK.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Technical Assistance Facility will build LMIC capacity and establish lasting links with UK institutions and businesses. This includes:
i.	A domestically focused offer to national governments through embedded technical support to develop and implement strategies for emerging technologies to create sustainable and innovation positive technology ecosystems, identify and mitigate risks to systems and values presented by technology supply chains, and facilitate locally driven demand for establishing tech-focused partnerships with UK business/investors.    
ii.	Targeting increased activity in multilateral fora providing national governments with embedded technical support to actively participate in the evolution of international technology governance and, where appropriate, take on regional leadership roles to encourage wider LMIC country participation.
iii.	Strengthen participation by other ecosystem actors such as civil society, provide support for advocacy on open, responsible, secure and resilient principles, and translate evidence and research into action.
iv.	Support/ inform negotiations on infrastructure and enable greater market access / purchasing power by supporting regional initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
